MIRIX (modified / ported from MIRIX)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The XIAR memory core (core/rust/crates/xiar-memory and related crates) is a
Rust port of, and contains material modified from, MIRIX:
  https://github.com/Mirix-AI/MIRIX
  Copyright Mirix-AI and MIRIX contributors.
  The upstream LICENSE file also carries "Copyright 2023, Letta authors"
  (MIRIX derives from Letta, formerly MemGPT).
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0; full text in
  core/rust/prompts/mirix/LICENSE).
Upstream commits used as porting targets: 8cb06a62 (main, 2026-08-20) and
f7e75fc3 (desktop-agent, 2025-12-03; includes contributions merged from pull
request #92, also Apache-2.0).
Changes: the MIRIX Python code (schemas, ORM, memory managers, tools, search,
filter tags, raw/experience memory, timezone helpers) was rewritten in Rust;
SQLAlchemy/pgvector storage was replaced by redb + xiar-qdrant-edge; multi-
tenant scoping, sealing and the governance ledger were added. Files derived
from MIRIX say so in their module documentation ("Ported from MIRIX ...",
"Derived from MIRIX ..."). The Rust port is distributed under
AGPL-3.0-or-later (as permitted by Apache-2.0 section 4), with MIRIX's
copyright and licence notice preserved here and in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.
The original MIRIX prompts are NOT relicensed: they stay under Apache-2.0 in
core/rust/prompts/mirix/ (see core/rust/prompts/mirix/NOTICE.md).

